  "relevance_note": "The cohort paper describes two HA20 patients, each tied to a specific TNFAIP3 variant: 'The genetic sequencing yielded p.R271X of the TNFAIP3 gene in one patient and p.R45X in the other one'.",
  "method_note": "Read the whole paper manually; a short Python script in my scratch directory only assembled the JSON (no table was transcribed by script). Scope: the study genotyped 288 patients and diagnosed 79 with monogenic AIDs; only the two HA20 patients are in scope, all other cohort members get no rows. The paper gives no labels, so both are 'unnamed person <k>'. Labels are anchored on the sentence that ties each person to a variant ('p.R271X of the TNFAIP3 gene in one patient and p.R45X in the other one'): unnamed person 1 = p.R271X carrier, unnamed person 2 = p.R45X carrier. Table 2 lists the variants in the opposite order ('p.R45X, p.R271X'), so another extractor might number them the other way. Per-patient facts that cannot be linked to either variant carrier and were therefore NOT assigned: 'One patient was diagnosed as Behçet disease previously and the other one was diagnosed with undifferentiated connective tissue disease'; 'Hashimoto′s thyroiditis was also found in one patient' (so autoimmune thyroiditis is 'not reported' for both); Table 2 group-level 'Main clinical findings' for A20 deficiency (n = 2) 'Fever, rash, arthralgia, mucosal ulcers, bowel inflammation, CTD' (no per-patient counts); Table 2 age at onset '4 (0–8)' (median, range, unit not stated). Sex 'female' for both is deduced from Table 2 'Gender (male: female)' = '0:2' for n = 2. Recurrent oral ulcer is recorded from 'both suffered from recurrent oral ulcer', which covers each of the two patients by name of the group ('our patients'). Ethnicity 'Chinese' and 'no consanguinity' are statements about all children in the study, applied to both. Treatment is a group statement ('For Blau syndrome, DADA2 and HA20 patients, we initiated anti-TNF-α therapies'); it does not say each HA20 patient received it. Not used as evidence (study inclusion criteria): 'They all had persistently or intermittently elevated inflammation indices with no evidence of malignancy or infection', so elevated inflammatory markers and infections stay 'not reported'. Zygosity left 'not reported': Table 2 'Inheritance' = 'AD' is the disease's mode of inheritance, and the paper does not say heterozygous for these patients. Variant class not stated by the authors. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients left null: the only prior-report statement concerns the out-of-scope NLRP12-AID cases ('which have been analyzed and reported previously (12)'), and the HA20 citation '(25, 26)' supports the variants' pathogenicity, not a prior description of these patients. Contradiction noted (not affecting in-scope rows): 'All of these AID patients are under regular follow-up' vs Table 3 case 8 'Death prior to treatment'; vital status not inferred.",
